efore you download Hugging Face repositories, you might wanna check the source and check the security scans, have your own security scans, whatever, that I'll get off of my soapbox the", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=1962", "end": 2060.385, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "2911d2506f5ebbd15139b98e0e4438e8c668cacb250b1018d0f191a9aab55a47", "start": 1962.21, "text": "That's kind of principle one, and certainly things that people are are, addressing from a variety of angles. Thing two is these things are spawning so quickly. There there was likely no human that could have made decisions quick enough to r", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=2322", "end": 2391.82, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "2da2e8fd6520b6f0deddce3f8517cdf6892b866433cd3524c160bad4206bea4e", "start": 2322.485, "text": "They were blocked because of the guardrails associated with that model, which they did not have control over. So they didn't control whether those guardrails were on or off. They were just uploading to the platform itself, which had an opin", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "Uncategorized", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=1", "end": 75.865005, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "00d1f64b9e50371a6803968ceffc8af49777037930ad3b5d22b0df5dc16af29b", "start": 1.76, "text": "Welcome to the Practical AI Podcast, where we break down the real world applications of artificial intelligence and how it's shaping the way we live, work, and create. Our goal is to help make AI technology practical, productive, and access", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://share.transistor.fm/s/9d74230b#t=768", "end": 854.085, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "34b280631d8b09f8d5f0d90fc11fdf964e8d2a79a7ae5f